    "turn_text": "I find is that, you know, as Nevada and myself, seeing your career expand and grow. I know you started out in Louisiana, that's one of my favorite places in New Orleans, and then of course coming to Las Vegas, being on the cutting edge of all the transportation projects for probably 15, 16 years in Nevada. You've experienced one of the fastest growing communities in the country, if not in the world, in southern Nevada, with the expansion of the Las Vegas Valley, north Las Vegas, Henderson, Boulder, Mesquite area. But you're uniquely qualified with what's happening in Washoe County right now. also experience massive growth, shortage of infrastructure because of the demands, which is a positive thing. But you experienced that in Southern Nevada in the 90s and in the 2000s. So you are uniquely qualified because of your experience. So explain your vision on From your experience, from transit to highways and byways, what you do different compared to the rest of the country.",
