    "turn_text": "It really is, and it's exciting, literally there is a bridge, but it really is a bridge to connecting the university with the community, the commercial part of the community. Lee, you and I chat many times about leadership style and what's happening. Here we're literally in the shadow, I guess is the term of the US Capitol today, right across the street. And we talk about leadership and some of the challenges today for federal government, but how the local government's role is really expanding and how more important today than it is ever for local governments. So from your perspective, from Washington all the way to Washoe County, What do you see as a leader of the future in transportation? What needs to happen",
